    "title": "Why the Kitchen Is the Hardest Part of a Restaurant Move - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 days ago Moving a dining room takes an afternoon. Chairs stack, tables flip, the framed photo of the original storefront goes into a moving blanket, and nobody loses sleep. The kitchen? Totally different animal. Heaviest, priciest, most finicky gear in the business — and half of it’s plugged into gas, water, and power that aren’t going anywhere. Do one move and you’ll say what everyone says: front of house, one day. Back of house, one month. Read full article",
